---

# Project Layout

Use src layout.

Example

src/

    cqros/

        core/

        data/

        exchange/

        research/

        ...

Never place production code outside src/cqros.

---

# Imports

Always use absolute imports.

Correct

from cqros.core.logging import get_logger

Incorrect

from ..core.logging import get_logger

Avoid relative imports.

---

# Package Structure

Every package contains

__init__.py

Public API

Private modules begin with underscore when appropriate.

---

# Path Handling

Always use pathlib.Path.

Never concatenate paths manually.

Correct

DATA_DIR / "btc.parquet"

Incorrect

DATA_DIR + "/btc.parquet"

---

# Configuration

Read configuration through CQROS configuration system.

Never read YAML directly inside business logic.

Never hardcode paths.

Never hardcode exchange URLs.

Never hardcode thresholds.

---

# Time

Timezone aware only.

UTC only.

Never use naive datetime objects.

Exchange timestamps converted immediately to UTC.

---

# Randomness

Always control random seeds.

Record seed in metadata.

Research must be reproducible.

---

# Serialization

Use

Parquet

JSON

YAML

Avoid Pickle unless explicitly required.

If Pickle is used,

record version,

hash,

and compatibility.

---

# Concurrency

Use async only for

REST

WebSockets

Network IO

Disk IO

Use multiprocessing for CPU-intensive workloads when justified.

Avoid unnecessary threading.

---

# Memory

Avoid unnecessary dataframe copies.

Prefer lazy evaluation in Polars.

Stream large datasets where possible.

Avoid loading unnecessary columns.

---

# Performance

Profile before optimization.

Prefer vectorized operations.

Avoid Python loops over dataframe rows.

Batch expensive operations.

---

# Error Handling

Raise CQROS exceptions.

Wrap third-party exceptions when crossing package boundaries.

Never silently ignore failures.

---

# Logging

Every package uses CQROS logging.

Never print().

Log

startup

shutdown

warnings

errors

major state changes

Never log secrets.

---

